    "notes": [
      "lat and lon are decimal degrees: latitude first (north is positive), then longitude (west of Greenwich is negative). Map libraries such as Leaflet take them in that order, [lat, lon].",
      "Each period is one snapshot in time. The app shows one period every periodSeconds seconds while a replay is playing.",
      "A flight's lat,lon in each period is a placeholder point on the straight line from its origin airport to its destination airport; progress is how far along that line it is (0-100). Real flights follow curved paths.",
      "altitude is null when a flight is not reporting one; the page shows 'Not available'.",
      "departed and eta are fixed placeholder times and are not tied to the period clock.",
      "Live mode is not connected yet. A live API will later return the same kind of record for the current moment."
    ]
